  "transcript": "Canonical serialization rule: take the proposal artifact bytes exactly as given, canonically serialize as JSON with sorted keys and no whitespace, persist those exact bytes as proposal_canon.json in the run scratch dir, then compute hProposal = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json) and seed = SHA-256(hProposal + salt) (salt as provided by the engine). A third party can re-derive by hashing the same proposal_canon.json to reproduce hProposal, then hashing hProposal concatenated with the same salt to reproduce seedHex. Hash command evidence (conceptual, no execution claimed): sha256sum proposal_canon.json → hProposal; then sha256sum over (hProposal + salt) → seedHex."
